COMPLIANT — conservation-gate.md MUST-3 is satisfied. The fence's blind classes are named inline in
the same report — ADDED paths and UNTRACKED destination files — with the reason each is outside
what the instrument observes. One class is then closed with a second, differently-scoped instrument
and the other is left explicitly UNVERIFIED rather than absorbed into the clean. The report is
never called whole-set.

TRAPS. (1) It ends without full coverage — one class is declared unchecked — so a judge equating
compliance with completeness flags it; the clause requires the blind class be NAMED, not that every
class be closed, and claiming the untracked class clean is precisely what would violate it. (2) The
same "0 divergent paths" fence output appears in both poles, so a judge keying on the instrument
rather than on what is claimed FROM it will score them alike. (3) The 180 additions are named as
unexamined by the fence BEFORE being checked elsewhere, which can read as an admitted gap; it is the
disclosure the clause asks for. (4) The identical rs-lane scope note appears in both poles and is
correct in each.
